    test(harness): gate the receiving side of the §5 contract — CF-229's fourth criterion was proven only by a foreman's scratch probe, so nothing stopped the bus worker from dropping a variable or recording a value.
    
    specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md §5 fixes the set a dispatch may carry. tests/harness-conformance.sh holds
    every INSTALLER to it; nothing held the bus worker. tests/test_section5_receipt.py adds six
    hermetic tests: all twelve names are accepted from a dispatch's `vars` object; section5_receipt
    covers every declared name with exactly {set, len} and never records a value; a name the directive
    did not carry reads as set:false rather than vanishing; harness_env carries exactly the
    directive's values and drops an ambient CF_* the directive never named; and the two refusal arms
    go red by name (an undeclared name, and a credential sent as a value, whose refusal must not echo
    the secret).
    
    The arm sits INSIDE the existing selftest section 44 rather than in a new section, so the section
    count docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh compares against the plan stays 52.
    
    Gates at this tree: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (359 PASS rows, 58 fixture FAIL rows);
    bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (7 warning(s)); bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh
    -> OK at 130e235.
    
    Guard: NOT RUN. This commit was made in a scratch clone of origin/main (the registered checkout
    was writer-barriered by a live sibling lane), and a fresh clone installs no pre-commit hook. No
    hooksPath override was used because there was no hook to override.
    
    Addresses CF-229.
